  <section><h2>Frequently asked questions about water heaters in Melissa</h2>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Who is the best water heater company in Melissa, TX?</h3><p>For 2026, our top pick is H2 Mechanical Services LLC, based in Melissa since 2013 and licensed (TACLB84965C) for both HVAC and water heater work. Masters Touch Plumbing Solutions, also Melissa-based with a Registered Master Plumber license, is a close second.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Is water heater work handled by plumbers or HVAC companies in Melissa?</h3><p>Both. Standard tank water heaters are typically a licensed plumber's job, while gas tankless conversions often involve mechanical contractors who also handle HVAC work, which is why this list overlaps with our Melissa plumbing ranking.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>How much does a water heater cost to replace in Melissa?</h3><p>A standard 40-50 gallon tank replacement runs $1,200-$2,800 installed in North Texas for 2026, with most like-for-like gas swaps landing between $1,300 and $1,900. Tankless conversions run $4,500-$10,000 once gas line and venting work are factored in.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Does DFW's hard water affect water heaters in Melissa?</h3><p>Yes. North Texas tap water commonly runs 10 to 17-plus grains per gallon of hardness, which accelerates scale buildup inside both tank and tankless units. Annual descaling flushes, typically $100-$200, meaningfully extend a water heater's service life.</p></div>
